Hi there!

My usual trouble #1 with wizards was that they got hungry
until they died -- now guess what -- my last wizard was
generated with a ring of slow digestion -- now that's something
to be happy about! What's more, this ring is cursed (by a
kobold shaman, I believe) -- does it only mean I can't take
it, or does it differ in some other manner from a normal
ring of slow digestion?
>> It is still normal, you just will be unable to take it off until you
find a scroll of remove curse.

It seems to work fine -- I'm satiated
all the time -- very nice for my wizard. :)
>> You can eat corpses.  That will help with your hunger.  The ring
just slows the hunger process, not eliminates it.

I explored the mines for a few levels,
including the level where there are a lot of guards and a few
shops (is that what you guys call 'minetown'?).
>> Yes

I found almost
nothing of value in the shops. I found an altar of my alignment
on... dlvl1 and when I came back there after my exploration
and offered only one corpse, I got awarded Magicbane. That's
my first artifact, so I'm quite excited about it.
>> Sacrificing at altars is always good.  If you got an artifact on the
first try, it was a 1 in a million happening.  Usually you have to sac
many corpses before getting anything.  Be wary of sacrificing on an
altar of a different alignment as you may convert it to your alignment,
but you also may not and anger your god a little.

In desperation I read all the
scrolls I had, hoping to both identify them for later game
and to find a scroll of identify, but that didn't do much.
>> If you notice the effects of the things you are reading you can
figure out what they do.  Then you can #name or #call your item
according to what you think it is.  An example is you can engrave wands
in the floor, and they will give you a message usually, and many times
you can figure out what kind of wand it is by the message.  Plus
reading scrolls randomly can have detrimental effects if they are
cursed or even normal like teleport, etc.

I do not know the spell of identify. So how do I identify
my rings    /    potions/scrolls/wands quickly?
>> Identify is one of the difficulties of the game.  You just have to
find scrolls of identify.  Sometimes this takes a while.  You could
also get lucky and find a spellbook of identify.  Then you would know
the spell and could cast it, but they are rare.

Second of all -- I have St:12 and am constantly on the
verge of being Burdened. Having a few potions, scrolls,
books, wands, rings and daggers is the most I can afford.
>> Part of nethack is inventory management.  You don't need to carry
every little thing you find.  Unless you are using daggers all the
time, you only need 1, etc.  Str 12 is good for a wiz.  Keep pushing
boulders, etc if you want more str, or you can drink a potion of gain
ability or eat certain corpses.

I'm carrying all the wands    /    rings/scrolls/potions because
they are not identified. Is that the right thing to do?
>> You want to keep the items as once you identify them you may find
out if you had thrown them away, you threw away something really good.

Do I need to carry the books?
>> You can sell them if it is taking up too much space.

What about other potentially
useful items (I found a leash, a whistle, a towel, a blindfold,
a tin opener, etc.) -- am I supposed to carry it all with me?
>> Only if you want to... you might be better off selling them.

If not, how do I store them safely in some place?
>> A bag of holding will help you if you can get one.  Don't forget you
are a wizard not a big burly fighter.  If you could have magic AND
strength, the game would be unbalanced.

Third of all -- how do I acquire lower AC as a wizard?
>> You can use almost any non metal armor at no penalty to
spellcasting, and cloaks and rings help as well as boots, gloves, and
helms.

I had my AC at a measly 8 but unfortunately I put
on a cursed helmet of <something bad> and now have AC 10. Duh.
I realize this sucks -- how do I go about fixing it?
>> You need a scroll of remove curse.

Fourth, and last, of all -- is this Magicbane I got better
that my blessed +3 quarterstaff?
>> YES!

I know I can find a few
tables about it in the spoilers, but in real life -- will it
make sense to use this Magicbane instead of my quarterstaff?
If so, why? If not, why?
>> Magicbane is MUCH better than a regular staff, at ANY plus.  If you
want to see all of what it does, read the spoilers, because it does
quite a bit... too much to post here.

Do my abilities to use the Magicbane
rely on my dagger skill?
>> Yes

Can I have a shield in my other hand with
the Magicbane or with the quarterstaff? Does it make sense
for a wizard?
>> Not really.

Also, a few of my characters had died on the oracle
level after entering a room full of various animals.
This time there was no such room on the oracle level
-- how is it?
>> Room full of animals?  You sure it just was not alot of monsters?

OK, perhaps one more -- how do I stop my beloved tame large
cat from attacking peaceful characters, other than locking
it up or keeping it on a leash. Do characters like "peaceful
hill orc" or alike help you in any way or do they only
grunt on being #chatted to and ask for potions of full
healing? I.e, should I really prevent my pets from attacking
them, or let them kill them, pretending I don't notice and
pick the goodies?
>> Pets are your friends.  Let them attack unless you have a specific
reason not to, as it gives them XP and they will go up in level and be
able to help you much more, plus they need food, so the corpses will
help them survive.

thanks in advance, quite a few questions,
